1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,032
This is Allowance, a spending firewall for AI agents on Solana.

2
00:00:04,082 --> 00:00:10,002
In the next few minutes you'll see how to set it up, and what happens when your agent tries to overspend.

3
00:00:11,452 --> 00:00:14,148
AI agents can now pay for APIs over x402.

4
00:00:14,198 --> 00:00:17,631
But no company wants to hand a model an open wallet.

5
00:00:17,681 --> 00:00:24,530
Allowance puts the budget inside a Solana program, so the chain itself says yes or no to every payment.

6
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,451
Here's the flow. Your agent asks to pay.

7
00:00:28,501 --> 00:00:34,188
The program checks the session's caps, the merchant, its reputation, and the freeze switch.

8
00:00:34,238 --> 00:00:35,638
Then the chain answers.

9
00:00:35,688 --> 00:00:38,726
A yes moves USDC from your vault to the merchant.

10
00:00:38,776 --> 00:00:41,626
A no lands on-chain, with the rule that fired.

11
00:00:43,076 --> 00:00:49,477
The How it works page lists every rule the program checks, in order, and the error each one returns.

12
00:00:49,527 --> 00:00:52,122
So a refusal always names the exact rule.

13
00:00:53,572 --> 00:00:55,689
Click Launch app, and connect Phantom.

14
00:00:55,739 --> 00:00:58,199
Here we're viewing the demo vault read-only.

15
00:00:58,249 --> 00:01:02,534
The overview shows active sessions, today's spending, and the vault balance.

16
00:01:02,584 --> 00:01:04,416
Your Phantom wallet stays sealed.

17
00:01:04,466 --> 00:01:07,154
Agents can only spend what you put in the vault.

18
00:01:08,604 --> 00:01:13,106
Fund the vault from the Vault page, or send USDC to the vault address.

19
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:17,137
Only your wallet can withdraw, even while the vault is frozen.

20
00:01:17,187 --> 00:01:18,958
And this is the kill switch.

21
00:01:19,008 --> 00:01:23,314
Freeze blocks every payment, from every session, on-chain, at once.

22
00:01:24,764 --> 00:01:27,161
Next, create a session for your agent.

23
00:01:27,211 --> 00:01:31,283
Start the MCP server once, and it prints the agent's public key.

24
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:36,114
Paste it here, give the session a name, and choose how many hours it lasts.

25
00:01:37,564 --> 00:01:38,811
Now set the limits.

26
00:01:38,861 --> 00:01:47,273
In the demo, that's at most 0.05 USDC per payment, 2 USDC a day, and any unlisted service needs a reputation of at least 70.

27
00:01:47,323 --> 00:01:51,163
The panel on the right restates the rules in plain words.

28
00:01:51,213 --> 00:01:54,098
Sign with Phantom, and the session is live.

29
00:01:55,548 --> 00:02:03,226
The Sessions page lists every agent key, with its status, today's spending, its per-request cap, and when it expires.

30
00:02:04,676 --> 00:02:07,299
Open one to see its progress against each cap:

31
00:02:07,349 --> 00:02:12,239
the daily budget, each merchant's own cap, and the shared cap for unlisted merchants.

32
00:02:12,289 --> 00:02:14,970
You can revoke a session from here at any time.

33
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,412
Then connect Claude or Cursor.

34
00:02:18,462 --> 00:02:24,811
Add the Allowance MCP server to your config, with your Phantom address and the agent key path.

35
00:02:24,861 --> 00:02:31,346
Claude gets tools to check its allowance, pay x402 APIs, pay contacts, and ask you for approval.

36
00:02:32,796 --> 00:02:33,583
Now just ask.

37
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:37,769
When Claude calls a paid API, the program pays exactly the price.

38
00:02:37,819 --> 00:02:44,338
When a request breaks a rule, the chain refuses it, and Claude tells you which rule, with the numbers.

39
00:02:45,788 --> 00:02:49,515
Every result shows up in Activity, read straight from the chain.

40
00:02:49,565 --> 00:02:53,706
Each payment carries the agent's reason, and a link to its transaction.

41
00:02:55,156 --> 00:02:58,334
Here are the three rejections from the demo run.

42
00:02:58,384 --> 00:03:02,099
A 0.50 USDC report, refused as over the per-request cap.

43
00:03:02,149 --> 00:03:05,798
A poorly reviewed provider, refused for low reputation.

44
00:03:05,848 --> 00:03:10,370
And a payment tried while the vault was frozen, refused with Frozen.

45
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:15,419
When a payment is over the cap, the agent can ask you instead.

46
00:03:15,469 --> 00:03:17,773
The request waits on the Approvals page.

47
00:03:17,823 --> 00:03:21,186
An approval works once, for that merchant and that amount.

48
00:03:21,236 --> 00:03:24,658
Here, the same report was paid after the owner approved it.

49
00:03:26,108 --> 00:03:34,842
Merchants shows who your agents may pay, either listed in a session or let through by the reputation gate, with today's spending against each cap.

50
00:03:36,292 --> 00:03:39,997
And Contacts lets your agent pay people by name, like:

51
00:03:40,047 --> 00:03:44,865
pay my friend 0.05. It only works for addresses listed in the session.

52
00:03:44,915 --> 00:03:47,090
The program refuses anyone else.

53
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:49,544
That's Allowance:

54
00:03:49,594 --> 00:03:53,758
the spending firewall that lets companies switch agents on for x402.

55
00:03:53,808 --> 00:03:58,469
Even if the AI or the server were compromised, the chain enforces the rules.

56
00:03:58,519 --> 00:04:00,514
It's live on Solana devnet today.
